WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.005
Not every public detail creates the same risk.

00:00:03.005 --> 00:00:07.610
Evaluation begins with sensitivity: could the information expose identity, access,

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.000
location, relationships, internal operations, or security controls?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.290
Then consider who can use it, how easily it can be combined,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.000
and what harm could reasonably follow.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.914
Context changes risk.

00:00:16.914 --> 00:00:19.140
A generic technology name may be low sensitivity,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.480
while the same detail combined with an exposed service and unpatched version may require

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.000
action.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.518
A public office address differs from a private residence or precise routine.

00:00:27.518 --> 00:00:31.340
Aggregation risk occurs when individually ordinary details combine into a sensitive

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:31.985
picture.

00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:34.530
Usernames, photos, calendars, vendor references,

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.250
and technical records can reveal relationships or timing that no one source states

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.245
directly.

00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:43.555
Analysis should minimize unnecessary aggregation, especially about individuals.

00:00:43.555 --> 00:00:45.340
Assess timeliness and accuracy.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.935
Old records, cached pages, reused addresses,

00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:50.995
and abandoned profiles can misrepresent current conditions.

00:00:50.995 --> 00:00:55.025
Validate important findings with authoritative or independent sources and record when each

00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:56.000
source was observed.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.010
Separate relevant findings from noise.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.580
A useful finding connects to a legitimate security, privacy, safety,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.930
or business objective and has enough evidence to support action.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.995
Popularity, novelty, or personal curiosity are not measures of relevance.

00:01:07.995 --> 00:01:12.000
Prioritize by likelihood, potential impact, exposure, and confidence.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Describe uncertainty and avoid alarmist conclusions.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.880
Remediation should be proportionate: correct a stale page, restrict a document,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.000
secure an account, assign an asset owner,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
or investigate an exposed service through authorized internal processes.
